<td>GULF TREASURE</td>\n                <td>₦1,670.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>IBACHEM</td>\n                <td>₦1,670.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>DUPORT</td>\n                <td>₦1,670.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>WOSBAB</td>\n                <td>₦1,675.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>RAINOIL LAGOS</td>\n                <td>₦1,675.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>T.TIME</td>\n                <td>₦1,675.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>IBETO</td>\n                <td>₦1,675.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>PINNACLE</td>\n                <td>₦1,670.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            Market News\n        </h2>\n        \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Depot Prices Weekly Review: 17th–21st August 2026\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Nigeria’s downstream petroleum market recorded broad-based increases in depot prices between Monday, August 17 and Friday, August 21, 2026. The market also came under pressure from rising international crude prices, with oil trading close to $95 per barrel amid the continuing crisis around the Strait of Hormuz.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/depot-prices-weekly-review-17th21st-august-2026\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    CNG Fails to Cut Transport Fares as Nigerians Still Pay More\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Nigeria’s shift to compressed natural gas (CNG) has reduced fuel costs for some commercial transport operators. But the savings have yet to translate into cheaper fares for many commuters. The Federal Government introduced the CNG initiative after the removal of petrol subsidy.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/cng-fails-to-cut-transport-fares-as-nigerians-still-pay-more\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Brent Crude Nears $95 as Depot Prices Stay Elevated\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Brent crude was trading at $94.63 per barrel, up 0.91% , while WTI crude rose 0.55% to $87.31 per barrel. Iran warned Gulf states against supporting U.S. military operations, while Washington prepared additional economic measures against Tehran.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/brent-crude-nears-95-as-depot-prices-stay-elevated\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Iran Vows ‘Devastating’ Response as U.S. Threatens Toughest Sanctions\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Iran has warned that any fresh economic offensive by the United States would trigger a ‘devastating’ response. The warning came on Friday after US Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent said the administration would unveil details of its planned sanctions on Monday. The confrontation is also weighing on global oil markets, with crude prices heading for a second consecutive weekly gain.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/iran-vows-devastating-response-as-us-threatens-toughest-sanctions\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Atiku Proposes Targeted Refinery Subsidy Under 2027 Economic Plan\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Former Vice President Atiku Abubakar has proposed replacing Nigeria’s former petrol import subsidy with a targeted production-support programme for local refineries if he wins the 2027 presidential election. Atiku said the plan was designed to reduce energy costs while expanding domestic refining.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/atiku-proposes-targeted-refinery-subsidy-under-2027-economic-plan\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n\n        </body>\n\n        </html>\n        "
